                <pb facs="0663" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383/120: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-24T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2259. Your 3230, October 21, 5 p.m.</p>
                <p>You will insist that Mexican Government inform you definitely what steps have
                    been taken to effect release of Jenkins, and inform <pb facs="0664" n="579"
                        xml:id="pg579"/> Foreign Office that this Government expects Mexican
                    Government to take effective steps to obtain his release unharmed even if
                    payment by Mexico of indemnity demanded be necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
